Copyright (c) 2026 NishinoAkifumi. All rights reserved.

These terms govern your use of MyGravityMap (the "Software"). By installing or
using the Software you agree to be bound by them.

1. Grant of use
   Subject to these terms, the copyright holder grants you a non-transferable,
   non-exclusive right to use the Software free of charge, on any number of
   machines.

2. Restrictions
   You may not:
   (1) redistribute, publish, transmit to the public, lend, sell or sublicense
       the Software; or
   (2) modify, adapt or create derivative works of the Software.

3. Third-party software (exception to Section 2)
   The Software bundles software owned by third parties. The respective
   licenses of those components take precedence over these terms. See the
   bundled THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the full texts and attribution details.

   The restrictions in Section 2 do not apply to acts that those third-party
   licenses guarantee to users.

4. Map data
   Map tiles shown by the Software are fetched by your own device directly from
   the provider you select; they are not part of the Software. Map data is
   © OpenStreetMap contributors (Open Database License), and tile delivery is
   subject to the terms of CARTO, OpenFreeMap or VersaTiles respectively.
   Compliance with those terms is your responsibility.

5. Your data
   The Software does not transmit the location data you load outside your
   device. Processing happens entirely in the browser and results are stored
   only in your browser (IndexedDB). The copyright holder does not collect your
   location data and has no means of accessing it.

6. Reservation of rights
   All copyright and other rights in the Software are reserved by the copyright
   holder. These terms transfer no rights to you beyond those expressly granted.

7. No warranty
   The Software is provided "as is". The copyright holder makes no warranty of
   any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose and non-infringement.

8. Limitation of liability
   To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the copyright holder
   shall not be liable for any damages arising from the use of, or inability to
   use, the Software.

9. Governing law
   These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of
   Japan.
